...}.\n\nOn the student government ballot at Dusable High School, the six candidates for president are listed first, followed by the four candidates for vice president, followed by the five candidates for secretary and ending with the three candidates for treasurer. In how many ways can the candidates be listed on the ballot?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine the total number of ways the candidates can be listed on the ballot, we need to consider the order of the different positions and the number of candidates for each position. Specifically, we have:\n\n- 6 candidates for president\n- 4 candidates for vice president\n- 5 candidates for secretary\n- 3 candidates for treasurer\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5c878b9baa2439d9cb1febb9fdc8d1ee2b5e9f98ac065ac0ce8d61267e4c50a7"},"seconds":27.850921630859375,"seed":1136640197778094431,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total number of ways to list the candidates in the given order of positions on the ballot. The positions and their respective number of candidates are as follows:\n\n- 6 candidates for president\n- 4 candidates for vice president\n- 5 candidates for secretary\n- 3 candidates for treasurer\n\nThe total number of ways to arrange the candidates is the product of the number of ways to arrange the candidates within each position, since the candidates within each position can be arranged independently of the others.\n\nThe number of ways to arrange the 6 candidates for president is \\(6!\\) (6 factorial). The number of ways to arrange the 4 candidates for vice president is \\(4!\\). The number of ways to arrange the 5 candidates for secretary is \\(5!\\). The number of ways to arrange the 3 candidates for treasurer is \\(3!\\).\n\nThe total number of arrangements is given by the product of these factorials:\n\\[\n6! \\times 4! \\times 5! \\times 3!\n\\]\n\nCalculating each factorial, we get:\n\\[\n6! = 720, \\quad 4! = 24, \\quad 5! = 120, \\quad 3! = 6\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply these values together:\n\\[\n720 \\times 24 \\times 120 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(720 \\times 24\\):\n\\[\n720 \\times 24 = 17280\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(17280 \\times 120\\):\n\\[\n17280 \\times 120 = 2073600\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate \\(2073600 \\times 6\\):\n\\[\n2073600 \\times 6 = 12441600\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of ways the candidates can be listed on the ballot is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12441600}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{12441600}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total number of ways to list the candidates in the given order of positions on the ballot. The positions and their respective number of candidates are as follows:\n\n- 6 candidates for president\n- 4 candidates for vice president\n- 5 candidates for secretary\n- 3 candidates for treasurer\n\nThe total number of ways to arrange the candidates is the product of the number of ways to arrange the candidates within each position, since the candidates within each position can be arranged independently of the others.\n\nThe number of ways to arrange the 6 candidates for president is \\(6!\\) (6 factorial). The number of ways to arrange the 4 candidates for vice president is \\(4!\\). The number of ways to arrange the 5 candidates for secretary is \\(5!\\). The number of ways to arrange the 3 candidates for treasurer is \\(3!\\).\n\nThe total number of arrangements is given by the product of these factorials:\n\\[\n6! \\times 4! \\times 5! \\times 3!\n\\]\n\nCalculating each factorial, we get:\n\\[\n6! = 720, \\quad 4! = 24, \\quad 5! = 120, \\quad 3! = 6\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply these values together:\n\\[\n720 \\times 24 \\times 120 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(720 \\times 24\\):\n\\[\n720 \\times 24 = 17280\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(17280 \\times 120\\):\n\\[\n17280 \\times 120 = 2073600\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate \\(2073600 \\times 6\\):\n\\[\n2073600 \\times 6 = 12441600\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of ways the candidates can be listed on the ballot is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12441600}\n\\]","id":"counting_and_probability:329"}
